# generic_instance_from_use - a generic enum's variant is the instance its use names: a variant argument takes the instance its parameter has once the call's type arguments are bound (`first_ok(Result::Ok(4), 9)` for `r: Result<T, T>`), and type arguments written on a variant call name it (`Result::Ok::<i32, i32>(4)`).
